WEBVTT

00:00.805 --> 00:04.035
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.135 --> 00:07.404
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.438 --> 00:10.974
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.351 --> 00:14.319
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.354 --> 00:17.823
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:17.857 --> 00:21.126
♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪

00:21.160 --> 00:22.694
♪ All the things that make us

00:22.729 --> 00:24.062
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.097 --> 00:25.735
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.774 --> 00:38.043
<i>We now return
to Captain Central America.</i>

00:41.080 --> 00:42.714
It worked!

00:42.749 --> 00:44.516
<i>Gracias.
What are my powers?</i>

00:44.550 --> 00:45.951
Oh, yeah. It's weird.

00:45.985 --> 00:48.286
You're, like, really good
at painting my living room.

00:48.321 --> 00:50.288
Up, up, and get it done
by Saturday.

00:50.323 --> 00:51.757
We're having a party.

00:51.791 --> 00:53.825
Hey, Brian. Can you come
in here a sec?

00:53.860 --> 00:55.293
Sure, Peter,
what's up?

00:55.328 --> 00:56.695
You're a well-read guy, right?

00:56.729 --> 00:59.031
Well, I don't know. I guess
when I read my Henry David,

00:59.065 --> 01:00.632
I tend to be
pretty Thoreau.

01:00.667 --> 01:02.187
Shut up!
Yeah, 'cause, you see,

01:02.201 --> 01:04.036
I been reading this
novel about three guys,

01:04.070 --> 01:05.237
happen to be pigs, uh,

01:05.271 --> 01:07.105
that decide to
build their own houses.

01:07.140 --> 01:09.574
So, now, one of 'em builds
his house out of straws.

01:09.609 --> 01:11.977
Right? Now, how the hell do
you build a house out of straws?

01:12.011 --> 01:13.712
And-and three pigs
living together?

01:13.746 --> 01:15.814
Gay. You know?
And so's the wolf.

01:15.848 --> 01:17.949
He's chasing pigs and
blowing everything in sight.

01:17.984 --> 01:19.351
Peter,
what are you doing?

01:19.385 --> 01:21.420
I'm just getting ready for bed.
What's wrong?

01:21.454 --> 01:23.955
You're-you're naked.
I'm-I'm right here.

01:23.990 --> 01:25.357
Who cares? You're my dog.

01:25.391 --> 01:27.092
Everybody gets naked
in front of their dog.

01:27.126 --> 01:28.427
Besides, you're always naked,

01:28.461 --> 01:30.762
except for when Lois dresses
you up in that rain gear.

01:30.797 --> 01:32.431
Okay, everyone
in the car!

01:32.465 --> 01:34.299
We're going
to Martha's Vineyard!

01:34.333 --> 01:36.735
Do I have to wear this on the ferry?
Yes, you do.

01:36.769 --> 01:38.103
What about Peter?

01:38.137 --> 01:39.604
Why-why doesn't he
have to wear this crap?

01:39.639 --> 01:41.339
Peter's
in his crate.

01:41.374 --> 01:42.607
I'm actually relieved.

01:42.642 --> 01:44.776
The ferry would be
overstimulating.

01:50.249 --> 01:52.217
Mama!

01:52.251 --> 01:54.553
What are you doing
out of your box?

01:54.587 --> 01:56.221
Hey, Megan.
Oh, hey, guys.

01:56.255 --> 01:57.823
Wait, did you
just call me Megan?

01:57.857 --> 01:59.091
That's your name, isn't it?

01:59.125 --> 02:01.626
Actually, "Meg" is short
for something else.

02:01.661 --> 02:03.462
Peter, would you give this
to the nurse?

02:03.496 --> 02:04.830
Uh-huh.

02:08.468 --> 02:10.936
♪ Robots in disguise.

02:10.970 --> 02:12.938
Hey, did you guys hear
about that new kid?

02:12.972 --> 02:14.439
The emo Muslim?

02:16.476 --> 02:18.810
Death to America.

02:18.845 --> 02:21.012
No, this other guy,
Mike Pulaski.

02:21.047 --> 02:22.514
He's a complete psycho.

02:22.548 --> 02:24.583
I heard he knifed a kid
on the playground,

02:24.617 --> 02:26.051
then beat up the knife.

02:26.085 --> 02:29.187
<i>I heard he can watch Friday
Night Lights without crying.</i>

02:29.222 --> 02:30.522
I heard the volleyball team's

02:30.556 --> 02:32.257
playing a tournament
in San Diego.

02:32.291 --> 02:34.693
There's a lot
of exciting stuff going on.

02:45.772 --> 02:47.239
Man, he looks mean.

02:47.273 --> 02:48.774
You're very judgmental
lately.

02:48.808 --> 02:50.408
I don't like this Brandon.

02:50.410 --> 02:53.478
The best way to disarm a
bully is to befriend him.

02:53.513 --> 02:55.647
Watch and learn.

02:55.681 --> 02:57.649
Hey, what's up,
my main man?

02:57.683 --> 02:59.417
Listen, if you ever
need the scoop

02:59.452 --> 03:01.820
on the local babe scene,
just ask.

03:01.854 --> 03:03.455
Yeah, I'll do that.

03:11.397 --> 03:13.398
Awesome.

03:19.272 --> 03:22.073
♪ Doo doo doo doo doo,
taking a shower ♪

03:22.108 --> 03:25.076
♪ Taking a little break
to bite at the water... ♪

03:28.881 --> 03:30.115
Ah!

03:30.149 --> 03:31.650
Oh, hey, Brian.
Don't worry,

03:31.684 --> 03:33.652
there's no blade in the razor
'cause I'm learning.

03:33.686 --> 03:35.654
Peter, what the hell?!
What? What's the matter?

03:35.688 --> 03:37.722
What do you mean what's the
matter? You're completely naked!

03:37.757 --> 03:39.558
I told you I'm not
comfortable with that!

03:39.592 --> 03:41.760
Brian, I can get nude
whenever I want, all right?

03:41.794 --> 03:44.429
This is my home,
and a man's home is his castle.

03:44.463 --> 03:46.631
Halt, wench!

03:46.666 --> 03:47.899
State your business.

03:47.934 --> 03:49.968
Peter, will you please
put down the drawbridge?

03:50.002 --> 03:51.903
I got a car
full of groceries.

03:51.938 --> 03:53.972
Hmm. Anything else?

03:54.006 --> 03:55.807
I also went
to the video store

03:55.842 --> 03:58.710
<i>and got Garfield:
A Tail of Two Kitties.</i>

04:05.384 --> 04:07.352
Hey, you guys want
to sleep over this weekend?

04:07.386 --> 04:10.488
My moms are going out of town to
a scrapbooking-clambake retreat.

04:10.523 --> 04:12.023
What are they
gonna do there?

04:12.058 --> 04:15.093
They'll just be scissoring stuff
and eating clams all weekend.

04:15.127 --> 04:16.728
Sure, sounds grea...

04:41.320 --> 04:43.121
Oh...

04:43.155 --> 04:45.991
fudge.

04:46.025 --> 04:47.993
<i>Only I didn't say "fudge."</i>

04:48.027 --> 04:49.928
<i>I said.</i>

04:49.962 --> 04:51.997
Oh, my God!
I'm so sorry!

04:52.031 --> 04:53.665
What's your name, dude?

04:53.699 --> 04:55.166
Meg Griffin!

04:55.201 --> 04:57.035
3:00, Friday.

04:57.069 --> 05:00.105
I will destroy you.

05:01.440 --> 05:03.074
Chris, you have
my back, right?

05:03.109 --> 05:05.143
I don't know.
Let me check.

05:05.177 --> 05:05.875
Yeah.

05:05.900 --> 05:07.755
Okay, I'm gonna need it
for the fight.

05:16.276 --> 05:18.377
We now return
to the Kentucky Derby,

05:18.412 --> 05:19.846
where 90% of the audience

05:19.880 --> 05:21.914
roots for the horse
with the cutest name.

05:21.949 --> 05:23.449
And they're off!

05:23.484 --> 05:25.585
It's Battle Axe, followed by
Redbeard, followed by Bishop,

05:25.619 --> 05:27.086
followed by Smiling Pink Bear!

05:27.121 --> 05:28.521
Oh, my God, that's my horse!

05:28.555 --> 05:30.823
And on the outside,
here comes Tiny Kitten Kisses!

05:30.858 --> 05:31.824
No, no, that one!

05:31.859 --> 05:33.426
And here comes It's Bedtime!

05:33.460 --> 05:35.628
Oh, I do not like him.

05:38.766 --> 05:40.066
Meg, what's wrong?

05:40.100 --> 05:42.001
Some psycho just transferred
to my school,

05:42.035 --> 05:43.803
and he's going
to kill me!

05:46.206 --> 05:48.474
Boy, she must really
be PBS-ing, right?

05:48.509 --> 05:49.171
What?

05:49.196 --> 05:51.577
I mean, it's like, pop
a couple of tampons, you know?

05:51.578 --> 05:53.880
Stewie, do you even know
what a menstrual cycle is?

05:53.914 --> 05:55.348
Uh, yeah, Brian.

05:58.318 --> 06:01.320
It a good way to get around
town, that's what it is.

06:06.026 --> 06:07.660
Oh, good,
you're alone.

06:07.694 --> 06:09.729
Hey, Lois.
Why are you wearing a robe?

06:09.763 --> 06:12.632
Well, I heard about how Peter's
making you see him naked lately,

06:12.666 --> 06:17.069
so I thought the only way to get
even is for you to see me naked.

06:17.104 --> 06:18.805
Wh... Really?
Yeah.

06:18.839 --> 06:20.273
It only seems fair.

06:20.307 --> 06:22.608
You know what, that makes sense
to me. I mean...

06:22.643 --> 06:24.610
All right, here we go.

06:28.582 --> 06:30.349
You thought you were
gonna see my wife's penis,

06:30.384 --> 06:32.251
but, no, it's mine!

06:32.286 --> 06:34.754
You idiot!

06:39.126 --> 06:40.459
Good morning, students.

06:40.494 --> 06:42.962
This is Principal Shepherd
with the morning announcements.

06:42.996 --> 06:45.965
Remember that all wagers on
Friday's Meg Griffin slaughter

06:45.999 --> 06:48.367
must be on my desk by Thursday.

06:48.402 --> 06:51.237
Also, Zack Morris,
if you could stop freezing time

06:51.271 --> 06:54.106
to talk to the camera,
the day would go a lot faster.

06:54.141 --> 06:55.908
Oh, my God, you guys,
what am I gonna do?

06:55.943 --> 06:57.844
That psycho
is going to kill me.

06:57.878 --> 07:00.046
Meg, you've got to find a way
out of this fight.

07:00.080 --> 07:02.715
Yeah, Meg. You can do it.
You're a smart woman,

07:02.749 --> 07:04.717
and women can do
anything nowadays.

07:04.751 --> 07:05.918
I guess you're right.

07:05.953 --> 07:08.120
It's not
like it's the 1950s.

07:08.155 --> 07:10.089
So I see you graduated number one

07:10.123 --> 07:12.158
in your class from Princeton.
That's right.

07:12.192 --> 07:15.161
And I'm certified as an accountant and
also have a law degree.

07:15.195 --> 07:16.762
That's all very impressive.

07:16.797 --> 07:19.031
We'll keep you in mind.

07:19.066 --> 07:22.368
Let's see, Pointy Boobs,
Medium-Pointy Boobs,

07:22.402 --> 07:24.770
Not-So-Pointy Boobs.

07:24.805 --> 07:26.772
That's a shame.

07:30.177 --> 07:33.679
Hey, Mom, I need to transfer
to a different school.

07:33.714 --> 07:36.883
Meg, we've been over this.
Just because a Facebook page

07:36.917 --> 07:40.052
has over 2,000 likes doesn't
mean you have to kill yourself.

07:40.087 --> 07:42.221
I-It's not that.
Mom, please?

07:42.256 --> 07:43.489
There's other schools.

07:43.523 --> 07:46.092
Carlisle Academy leads the state
in teen pregnancies.

07:46.126 --> 07:48.261
So... I might
meet somebody.

07:48.295 --> 07:50.429
Meg, Carlisle Academy's
a private school.

07:50.464 --> 07:51.764
We can't afford it.

07:51.798 --> 07:53.900
Don't you remember how much
money your father wasted

07:53.934 --> 07:56.869
so he could make grand
staircase entrances?

07:58.639 --> 08:00.006
Hey, is Peter here?

08:00.040 --> 08:01.340
Hang on.

08:01.375 --> 08:02.441
Peter!

08:02.476 --> 08:04.176
Why, Glenn Quagmire.

08:04.211 --> 08:06.679
It's been 10 years
if it's been a day.

08:14.187 --> 08:16.088
I figured out how to get out
of this fight.

08:16.123 --> 08:18.257
All I have to do
is get expelled.

08:18.292 --> 08:20.793
That sex tape I released
should be everywhere by now,

08:20.827 --> 08:23.329
and then they'll have
to kick me out of the school.

08:26.700 --> 08:28.567
Come on! Really?

08:29.870 --> 08:31.203
Ooh.

08:33.707 --> 08:35.007
You know what?

08:35.042 --> 08:36.375
Good for her.

08:40.414 --> 08:42.548
Hey, guys, you four
are pretty much

08:42.582 --> 08:43.950
the toughest guys
in school, right?

08:43.984 --> 08:46.552
What would it take to get
you to beat up Mike Pulaski?

08:46.586 --> 08:48.621
Mental Mike?
Are you kidding?

08:48.655 --> 08:50.623
Come on, guys,
I'll do anything.

08:50.657 --> 08:52.558
I-I'll give you
a Swallow Friday.

08:52.592 --> 08:54.226
You mean
a Follow Friday?

08:54.261 --> 08:55.628
Oh...

08:55.662 --> 08:57.563
I've been doing
Twitter all wrong.

08:57.597 --> 08:59.732
Okay, okay.
I-I'll just pay you.

08:59.766 --> 09:01.734
Oh, yeah? Well,
you're looking at 1,000 bucks

09:01.768 --> 09:03.002
for something like that.

09:03.036 --> 09:05.004
$1,000? All right.

09:05.038 --> 09:07.406
But it's gonna be hard
to get that kind of money.

09:07.441 --> 09:09.675
I mean, I'm not Judge Judy.

09:09.710 --> 09:11.344
Hi, I'm Judge Judy.

09:11.378 --> 09:15.348
I get paid $45 million a year to
yell at people who have nothing.

09:15.382 --> 09:18.751
Now here's an ad about
a fat-people disease you have.

09:23.423 --> 09:26.592
<i>We now return to B.E.T. E.T.</i>

09:26.626 --> 09:28.728
Don't you need
to phone home?

09:28.762 --> 09:31.063
Nah, I do it later.

09:34.167 --> 09:35.267
Brian Griffin?

09:35.302 --> 09:36.435
Uh, yeah, that's me.

09:36.470 --> 09:37.470
Here you go.

09:39.973 --> 09:41.540
Aah! Oh, God!

09:41.575 --> 09:43.609
What's in the
box, Brian?

09:43.643 --> 09:45.945
I got you good!

09:45.979 --> 09:48.347
I don't feel right.
I want it back.

09:53.020 --> 09:54.420
What's going on?

09:54.454 --> 09:56.088
Did that kid from
the future come back?

10:02.129 --> 10:04.563
Oh, no!

10:07.000 --> 10:09.702
Meg, are you okay?

10:09.736 --> 10:12.638
You guys, I've tried
everything, but it's hopeless!

10:12.672 --> 10:14.106
He's going to kill me.

10:14.141 --> 10:16.909
I can already
picture my funeral.

10:20.447 --> 10:22.748
Thanks. Didn't want
to pay for the hole.

10:22.783 --> 10:24.483
This is such
a nightmare!

10:24.518 --> 10:26.285
At least I
have you guys.

10:26.319 --> 10:28.154
I don't know what I
would do without you.

10:28.188 --> 10:29.922
Yeah, uh, about that.

10:29.956 --> 10:32.158
Listen, Meg,
we decided that maybe it's best

10:32.192 --> 10:33.826
if you don't talk to us anymore.

10:33.860 --> 10:35.828
Yeah, we could be
targeted by association.

10:35.862 --> 10:37.897
I don't want to get
beaten up by a guy

10:37.931 --> 10:39.799
unless it's in a limo
after prom.

10:39.833 --> 10:43.102
So you're all gonna ditch me
when I need you most?

10:43.136 --> 10:44.703
Yeah, Meg,
it's natural selection.

10:44.738 --> 10:46.539
This is how it works
in the wild.

10:46.573 --> 10:48.374
Hey. Hey, how you doing?
Hey there.

10:48.408 --> 10:50.076
Hey. Nice spot, huh?
Oh, yeah.

10:50.110 --> 10:51.310
Oh, yeah, it's great.

10:51.344 --> 10:53.112
Especially 'cause of
that thing over there.

10:53.146 --> 10:55.114
You know what's in there? Corn.

10:55.148 --> 10:58.150
Really? Wow.
I could go for some corn.

11:01.621 --> 11:02.922
You're dark, Rog.

11:02.956 --> 11:04.290
I don't care.

11:04.324 --> 11:05.591
Good luck, Meg.

11:05.625 --> 11:08.060
Now we must retreat
into the shadows.

11:11.631 --> 11:14.266
What am I gonna do?

11:14.301 --> 11:16.869
Sounds like you have
a pretty big problem, Meg.

11:16.903 --> 11:18.104
Huh?

11:19.473 --> 11:21.507
Mr. Quagmire?

11:21.541 --> 11:22.942
What are you doing in here?

11:22.976 --> 11:24.610
This is my base
of operations.

11:24.644 --> 11:25.644
Mr. Quagmire,

11:25.679 --> 11:26.912
the girls' gym class

11:26.947 --> 11:28.581
will be in the showers
in 20 minutes.

11:28.615 --> 11:29.748
Thank you, Shirley.

11:29.783 --> 11:31.283
She's been with
me 12 years.

11:31.318 --> 11:32.451
It's her birthday today.

11:32.486 --> 11:34.019
Didn't get her anything.

11:34.054 --> 11:36.255
So, I guess you heard
about the fight, huh?

11:36.289 --> 11:38.891
Oh, yeah, they're talking about
it in all the girls' bathrooms.

11:38.925 --> 11:40.059
I'm so dead.

11:40.093 --> 11:41.360
No, you're not,

11:41.394 --> 11:43.462
because I'm gonna help you
defeat Mike Pulaski.

11:43.497 --> 11:44.463
You are?

11:44.498 --> 11:45.631
That's right.

11:45.665 --> 11:46.799
Be at my house first
thing tomorrow morning,

11:46.833 --> 11:47.967
and we'll get started.

11:48.001 --> 11:49.902
Wow, thanks, Mr. Quagmire.

11:49.936 --> 11:52.271
Well, I better get home.

11:55.775 --> 11:58.077
What a good way
to get around town.

12:02.617 --> 12:05.485
Okay, Meg, you've got a bully
problem, and I'm gonna help you.

12:05.520 --> 12:07.854
But Mr. Quagmire,
why would you want to help me?

12:07.889 --> 12:09.823
Because I was once
in your shoes, Meg.

12:09.857 --> 12:12.592
I wasn't always the confident
guy you see before you.

12:12.627 --> 12:15.595
You see, I, too,
was terrorized by a bully.

12:15.630 --> 12:19.700
It was 1986, and the cola wars
were at a frenzy.

12:19.734 --> 12:22.803
<i>I was sitting in the RC section
of the cafeteria</i>

12:22.837 --> 12:24.504
<i>when Tracy Bellings approached.</i>

12:24.539 --> 12:27.140
Why aren't you drinking
Coke, you dork?

12:27.175 --> 12:28.909
Pepsi would also
be acceptable!

12:28.943 --> 12:31.078
It doesn't have
to be a two-cola system!

12:31.112 --> 12:33.847
RC is what keeps the big guys
on their toes!

12:33.881 --> 12:35.916
You know what "RC"
stands for, don't you?

12:35.950 --> 12:37.217
"Chicks Rule!"

12:37.251 --> 12:38.618
<i>She was dyslexic.</i>

12:38.653 --> 12:39.920
<i>Anyway, that was the beginning</i>

12:39.954 --> 12:41.922
<i>of a long,
abusive relationship.</i>

12:41.956 --> 12:44.291
<i>It's one thing if you put
your penis inside-out</i>

12:44.325 --> 12:45.926
<i>in the safety
of your own bedroom,</i>

12:45.960 --> 12:48.095
<i>but to have it done
in the cafeteria...</i>

12:48.129 --> 12:50.497
<i>To this day,
I can't have sex with a woman</i>

12:50.531 --> 12:53.233
<i>against her will
without thinking about rape.</i>

12:53.267 --> 12:55.102
And that's
why I'm gonna help you, Meg.

12:55.136 --> 12:56.470
I never faced my bully.

12:56.504 --> 12:58.338
I don't want you
to make the same mistake.

12:58.373 --> 12:59.406
But how?

12:59.440 --> 13:00.640
Over the years,

13:00.675 --> 13:02.542
I've tested the limits
of the human body.

13:02.577 --> 13:05.212
How much it can stuff in,
swallow or choke on.

13:05.246 --> 13:06.713
How a scrotum can be stretched

13:06.748 --> 13:09.149
into a makeshift sail
if stranded at sea.

13:09.183 --> 13:11.585
All this knowledge is gonna
help you win your fight.

13:11.619 --> 13:13.019
Oh, thanks, Mr. Quagmire.

13:13.054 --> 13:14.955
I'll take any help I can get.

13:14.989 --> 13:16.256
I haven't been this scared

13:16.290 --> 13:18.425
since my dad stopped showering
for six months.

13:18.459 --> 13:19.960
Great meatloaf, Mom.

13:19.994 --> 13:21.428
Thanks, honey.

13:21.462 --> 13:22.763
Hungry!

13:22.797 --> 13:24.131
Hungry!

13:24.165 --> 13:25.966
Pour food on my pile!

13:26.000 --> 13:28.068
Okay, Peter, here you go.

13:28.102 --> 13:30.370
Mmm. I will assimilate
this new smell

13:30.405 --> 13:33.540
into the larger Borg
of my smells.

13:38.346 --> 13:39.913
Oh, by the way,
Rupert, good news.

13:39.947 --> 13:41.581
I pooped out your bow tie.

13:41.616 --> 13:42.816
Gaah!

13:42.850 --> 13:44.084
Geez, what the hell, Brian?!

13:44.118 --> 13:45.252
I can't take it anymore!

13:46.454 --> 13:47.687
